  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry conditions persist through the end of the week \nas temperatures gradually increase.\n\nNorthwest to northeast winds will continue to diminish the\nremainder of the day. Highs are topping out near average. Broad\nhigh pressure will build over the central Plains in the upper\nlevels, while transitioning to a surface high pressure over the\nmid-Atlantic. This ridge will influence dry conditions and\ngradually increasing temperatures through the rest of the week.\nPlenty of sunshine each day with highs approaching the middle to\nupper 60s to near 70 by Friday across the region. Lows at night\nwill remain in the 30s to 40s through the week. One caveat to\nthe prolonged dry conditions and warming temperatures could\nhave implications on fire weather (see fire weather section \nbelow). \n\nLooking towards next weekend, it is still looking quite dry at\nthis point, but there are some hints at some activity in both\nbranches of the jet stream going into early next week. At this\njuncture, not seeing any significant precipitation potential.\nThe two indications of possible precipitation chances will be a\ntrough of low pressure extending northwestward from a coastal\nlow near the Carolina Coast and an approaching cold front from\nthe Ohio Valley. As of now, there are only slight chances to\nchances of rain showers Saturday night into Sunday.",
